e flip and the `padding` clamp, THEN the content's offset from the anchor's origin (x and y) rounded to whole px, half away from zero (gpui's Positioner), so the box may end up half a px past the padding as the IDE's does. The Rust core (`/place_inset_overlay`, the layer manager's `inset` layers) and the TS twin (`placeInsetOverlay`) reproduce it exactly, Compose's SelectPopup replays it in dp; React and Solid land on it EXACTLY in headless Chromium (no `tolerancePx`; browser/overlay.test.ts, a pill Select, plain and searchable, replayed with the measured pill and popup): Solid's popper snaps after its shift and flip (`snapInset`), React moves the content from Radix's wraposper card'sonto full widthe box (`insetPopupNudge`).",
